"""NaN-propagation gap for min/max/clamp and the ops that decompose to them.

Compiler bug: Neuron's ``min``/``max``/``clamp`` -- and the reductions
``amax``/``amin``, the clamp-based activations ``hardsigmoid``/``celu``/``hardtanh``/
``relu6``, and the losses ``margin_ranking_loss``/``hinge_embedding_loss`` that
decompose to them -- follow IEEE-754 maxNum: a NaN operand is dropped and the non-NaN
operand / clamp bound is returned instead of propagating NaN. StableHLO requires NaN
propagation, so this is a compiler non-conformance, not a framework bug; do NOT mask
it with ``torch.where``. A spec-conformant NaN-propagating
``stablehlo.min``/``stablehlo.max`` in the compiler would clear every test below at
once (eager + compile) with zero framework overhead.

These 179 ``test x dtype`` parametrizations are consolidated here from the generic
accuracy / assertion / dtype buckets so the gap is tracked in one place as
unsupported. When the compiler fix lands, delete this whole group.
"""

